ore_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.025054680674495032,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":38.9,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00027000002,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Royal Bank of Canada operates as a diversified financial service company worldwide. Its Personal Banking segment offers home equity financing, personal lending, chequing and savings accounts, private banking, auto financing, mutual funds, GICs, credit cards, and payment products and solutions. The company's Commercial Banking segments provides lending, deposit and transaction banking products and services. Its Wealth Management segment provides a suite of wealth, investment, trust, banking, credit, and other solutions to clients; asset management products to institutional and individual clients; and asset and investor services to financial institutions, asset managers, and asset owners. The company's Insurance segment offers life, health, travel, wealth, annuities, property and casualty, and reinsurance advice and solutions; digital platforms; and independent brokers and partners, as well as client-led advice and solutions. The company's Capital Markets segment offers advisory and origination, sales and trading, lending and financing, and transaction banking services to corporations, institutional clients, asset managers, private equity firms, and governments. The company was founded in 1864 and is based in Toronto, Canada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David I. McKay | President, CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $6.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 101K people. Revenue per employee of $465K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Royal Bank Of Canada is a mega-cap financial services business with a $278.5B market cap on $47.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 91% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 83-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 5.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 40% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.40488723177777597},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 116% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","29 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Jefferies Financial Group Issues Pessimistic Forecast for Arteris (NASDAQ:AIP) Stock Price","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/jefferies-financial-group-issues-pessimistic-forecast-for-arteris-nasdaqaip-stock-price.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794012165.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance","legal"]},{"title":"Canada lost 4,700 jobs in October as unemployment rate climbs to 6.7%","source":"bnnbloomberg.ca","link":"https://www.bnnbloomberg.ca/business/2026/11/07/canada-lost-4700-jobs-in-october-as-unemployment-rate-climbs-to-67/","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794011446.205,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.572,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"TRREB Welcomes Federal Budget Measures to Boost Housing Supply and Affordability","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-est